---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# The distinct half of the locality guard (#971). `291` renamed every stateful
# pragma whose chain provably starts at a sequential source and ends at a
# terminal IN THIS BODY; anything still carrying the bare name could not be
# proved local, so its stream may have been handed in by a caller who made it
# parallel — `uniq(items.parallelStream())` — and the shared seen-set it would fuse into
# races across ForkJoin workers. This rule puts it back as the native call.
#
# It is the twin of `224`'s result, with the trigger changed: that rule fires
# when a `parallel()` call is visible in the method, this one when locality could
# not be established at all. The two compose — `224` runs first and takes the
# visibly parallel chains, `291` marks the provably local remainder, and whatever
# is left over arrives here.
#
# The reverted opcode carries `reverted ↦ Φ.true`, the fifth-operand marker
# `441`/`442`/`454` use: the recogniser that lifted this pragma is closed on the
# four-operand form jeo emits, so it cannot lift the result again and no cycle
# can spin. jeo ignores the extra binding when assembling.
name: unlocal-reverts-distinct
pattern: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.distinct,
    class ↦ 𝑒-class,
    stream-class ↦ 𝑒-stream-class
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
    i2 ↦ 𝑒-stream-class,
    i3 ↦ "distinct",
    i4 ↦ "()Ljava/util/stream/Stream;",
    i5 ↦ Φ.true,
    reverted ↦ Φ.true
  ⟧
